  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">World Health Organization (WHO) Assessed Contribution</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Australian Department of Health and Aged Care&apos;s assessed contribution (membership fees) to the World Health Organization (WHO) funds part of the WHO&#x2019;s regular budget and supports efforts in providing leadership on global health matters, shaping global health norms and standards, articulating evidence-based policy options, providing technical support to countries along with monitoring and assessing health trends. Assessed contributions paid to the WHO flow down to the WHO Western Pacific Regional Office. The WHO Western Pacific Regional Office plays a significant role in implementing health programmes across the Pacific and other countries within our region. 76% of the assessed contributions paid to the WHO are ODA-eligible.</narrative>
  </description>
